From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:27:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Escape the captions of media messages

Message bodies are HTML-escaped and their line breaks turned into <br>
before they are handed to purple, since WhatsApp is plain text and
purple expects HTML. The caption of an image, video or document took a
different path (purple_handle_attachment() and then
gowhatsapp_display_caption()) and reached the conversation unescaped:
a caption with "<", ">" or "&" was taken as markup, and its line breaks
were lost.

Escape the caption the same way as a message body before it is passed
to purple.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/hoehermann/purple-gowhatsapp/pull/295]
---
 handle_attachment.go | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/handle_attachment.go b/handle_attachment.go
index 1163f4b..eaae1f6 100644
--- a/handle_attachment.go
+++ b/handle_attachment.go
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ import "C"
 import (
 	"context"
 	"encoding/hex"
+	"html"
 	"mime"
 	"os"
 	"path/filepath"
@@ -131,6 +132,8 @@ func (handler *Handler) handle_attachment(message *waE2E.Message, id string, sou
 		}
 	}
 	if data_type != C.gowhatsapp_attachment_type_none {
+		// the caption is plain text like a message body, so escape it the same way before it reaches purple
+		caption = strings.ReplaceAll(html.EscapeString(caption), "\n", "<br>")
 		chat := source.Chat.ToNonAD().String()
 		sender := source.Sender.ToNonAD().String()
 		purple_handle_attachment(handler.account, chat, source.IsGroup, sender, caption, id, timestamp, data_type, filename, extension, mimetype, hash, length, downloadable)
